les a month.\nEvery 2 miles, the tires rotate 725 times.\nSo every mile, the tires rotate 725 / 2 = 362.5 times.\nFor 400 miles, the tires rotate 362.5 * 400 = 145000 times.\nEach tire can undergo 10,440,000 rotations before it needs to be replaced.\nSo the tires will last 10,440,000 / 145000 = 72 months.\nThere are 12 months in a year, so the tires will last 72 / 12 = 6 years.\nThe answer is 6.\n\nAnswer_16:\nThe jumbo bottle of shampoo costs $24.\nIt gives 120 washings.\nSo each washing costs 24 / 120 = 0.2 dollars.\nSince there are 100 cents in a dollar, each washing costs 0.2 * 100 = 20 cents.\nThe answer is 20.\n\nAnswer_17:\nThe shirt costs $25.\nThe shorts cost $35.\nSo the total cost is 25 + 35 = 60 dollars.\nThere is a 30% off sale, so the discount is 60 * 0.3 = 18 dollars.\nSo the total cost is 60 - 18 = 42 dollars.\nJoe originally had $50, so he has 50 - 42 = 8 dollars left.\nThe answer is 8.\n\nAnswer_18:\nIt takes 1/4 pound of butter to make 1 dozen croissants.\nSo it takes 1/4 * 12 = 3 pounds of butter to make 1 dozen croissants.\nJuan wants to make 4 dozen croissants a day for a week.\nSo he needs 3 * 4 * 7 = 84 pounds of butter.\nThe answer is 84.\n\nAnswer_19:\nIt costs $194 per meter to repave a street.\nMonica's street is 150 meters long, so it costs 194 * 150 = 29100 dollars.\nLewis' street is 490 meters long, so it costs 194 * 490 = 95260 dollars.\nSo it costs 95260 - 29100 = 66160 dollars more to repave Lewis' street.\nThe answer is 66160.\n\nAnswer_20:\nJohn gets initial funding of $100,000 for the first 5 months.\nEach month after that takes 50% more funding, so that is 1.5 times the initial funding.\nSo each month after the first 5 takes 1.5 * 100000 = 150000 dollars.\nThe research takes 10 times as long as the initial 5 months, so that is 10 * 5 = 50 months.\nSo the research takes 5 + 50 = 55 months.\nThe total funding is 100000 * 5 + 150000 * 50 = 1000000 dollars.\nThe answer is 1000000.\n\nAnswer_21:\nThe first player eats a 6-ounce steak